From f173efc8da89230834369ee49be5d5a5b3eaf85b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hermes Agent <hermes-agent@localhost>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:14:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/23] fix(kanban): scope claims to uid and refresh crash
 grace

Scope claim locality to host:uid:pid, translating the matching uid_map extent. Foreign and legacy claims are not liveness-probed or signalled as local; preserve TTL-based reclamation without termination. Crash grace follows the active task_runs start while tasks.started_at remains the first-start metric.

Rollout: drain dispatchers/workers and upgrade every process sharing the DB together; mixed versions are unsafe. Legacy host:pid claims are treated as foreign and reclaimed only after TTL without signalling, so a surviving worker can overlap after expiry. Rollback requires draining the new version before restoring all DB users to the old version. UID maps are parent-relative, not a universal host identity.
